Z||000006||Fiero5||12-08-2001||07:56 PM||||Man, you people are all paranoid.<P>"Can you say "fraud" boys and girls?<BR>I knew you could."<BR>Carefull, defamation of character is pretty serious also.<P>"Contact MS and have a re-print done... Not a happy road you're going down, dude"<BR>Tried that already. Called seven toll numbers (you know-"Oh, you need to call this department) at a cost I can't waite to see on my phone bill, not to mention the two calling cards I wiped out while trying to reach the right department from work also. Microsoft is if anything difficult to coordinate with in areas like this. If anyone has a more direct number I can call, it would be greatly appreciated. The MS rep I used to work with is gone and my company I worked for  (Market Makers) when I obtained my certification is also gone, so it's been pretty fun trying to get a replacement. NOT.<P>"its only fraud if you get caught."<BR>I don't remember ever saying I wanted to make up a fake illegal certificate, but I love how everyone so far has jumped to the conclusion that I must be trying to do something illegal.<P>"If I send mine, do I get the job?"<BR>It's not actually a new job as it is a new position, I am actually presenting a new idea to the school I work for and in my presentation it would be good to show them my qualifications backed up with copies of my certifications.<BR>And yes, I am MS certified. I am not that worried as if the SAU actually contacts MS, they will either get MS to verify that I am MS certified or unfortunately they will get the same idiotic run around I have gotten so far.<P>Sorry I wasted all your time and Cliff's space with this obvious unimportant thread. I guess taking everyone away from all the bickering, finger pointing, mustang/rice bashing and just so much more important all around flaming was just so very little of me.<P>Sheesh!<P>Steve||||reg||9
Z||000007||Mach10||12-08-2001||08:30 PM||||What about the instituition that you got the certificate from? We weren't flaming you... You just have to be REALLY careful when doing anything with MS documents and certificates. I used to be an authorized dealer. MS is RABID about some kinds of things...<P>Don't really have much I can tell you, other than to tell the employer the whole story. You DON'T have the certificate, because it has been lost, but that you ARE arranging for a replacement from MS. You DO have a certificate number, I can't see what the problem could be. ||||reg||12
